export default {"P000147":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Modules · predicate · <code>P000147</code></p><h3>Finite locally free module</h3><p>Each point of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Spec}R</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> has a principal open neighbourhood <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D(f)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> on which <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M_f</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is free of finite rank. The rank can vary with the point.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00NW\">Stacks 00NW · source and definition · Stacks 00NW · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00NW\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P000147\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000142":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Modules · predicate · <code>P000142</code></p><h3>Finite module</h3><p>An <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>-module <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is finite if some finite family of elements generates it over <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0518\">Stacks 0518 · source and definition · Stacks 0518 · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/algebra/#tag-0518\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P000142\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000143":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Modules · predicate · <code>P000143</code></p><h3>Finitely presented module</h3><p>There are nonnegative integers <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m,n</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and an exact sequence <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>→</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>→</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R^m\\to R^n\\to M\\to0</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0518\">Stacks 0518 · source and definition · Stacks 0518 · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/algebra/#tag-0518\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/xnotes/CA.pdf#page=52\">J. S. Milne, A Primer of Commutative Algebra, v4.03, Definition 12.2 (finite free presentation)</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P000143\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000153":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Modules · predicate · <code>P000153</code></p><h3>Flat module</h3><p>The functor <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mo>⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M\\otimes_R-</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> preserves exact sequences of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>-modules.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00HB\">Stacks 00HB · source and definition · Stacks 00HB · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00HB\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/xnotes/CA.pdf#page=45\">J. S. Milne, A Primer of Commutative Algebra, v4.03, §11, p. 45 (exactness of tensor)</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0251\">Stacks 0251 · common source definition · Stacks 0251 · (1) flat module</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-0251\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P000153\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000127":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000127</code></p><h3>Geometrically unibranch local ring</h3><p>The ring is unibranch, and the residue-field extension of the normalization of its reduction is purely inseparable.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BPZ\">Stacks 0BPZ · unibranch and geometrically unibranch local rings · Stacks 0BPZ · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/more-algebra/#tag-0BPZ\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P000127\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000146":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Modules · predicate · <code>P000146</code></p><h3>Locally free module</h3><p>Each point of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Spec}R</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> has a principal open neighbourhood <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D(f)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> on which <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M_f</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is free, possibly of infinite rank.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00NW\">Stacks 00NW · source and definition · Stacks 00NW · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00NW\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P000146\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000149":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Modules · predicate · <code>P000149</code></p><h3>Projective module</h3><p>The functor <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Hom</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Hom}_R(M,-)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is exact on the category of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>-modules.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05CE\">Stacks 05CE · source and definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/algebra/#tag-05CE\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/xnotes/CA.pdf#page=51\">J. S. Milne, A Primer of Commutative Algebra, v4.03, Definition 12.1 and its exact Hom characterization</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P000149\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000126":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000126</code></p><h3>Unibranch local ring</h3><p>The ring is local, its reduction is a domain, and the normalization of that domain in its fraction field is local.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BPZ\">Stacks 0BPZ · unibranch and geometrically unibranch local rings · Stacks 0BPZ · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/more-algebra/#tag-0BPZ\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P000126\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000106":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000106</code></p><h3>Valuation ring</h3><p>The ring is a domain and, in its fraction field, at least one of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> belongs to the ring for each nonzero <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00I9\">Stacks 00I9 · definition by domination · Stacks 00I9 · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00I9\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00IB\">Stacks 00IB · fraction-field criterion</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00IB\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P000106\">Open shared record</a></p></article>"};
